<title>LITHUANIA: LITHUANIA - BOURSE CAPITALISATION DOWN LAST WEEK.</title>
<headline>LITHUANIA - BOURSE CAPITALISATION DOWN LAST WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The capitalisation of the Vilnius</p>
<p>bourse dropped to 5.726 billion litas last week from 5.813</p>
<p>billion litas a week earlier, the stock exchange said on</p>
<p>Monday.</p>
<p>There were three trading sessions last week instead of five</p>
<p>because of public holidays.</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse statistics:</p>
<p>					     April 28-30   April 21-25</p>
<p>    Submitted orders		   10,405	  14,698</p>
<p>    Executed orders		    866	     983</p>
<p>Number of transactions on</p>
<p>    central market (CM)		802	     957</p>
<p>    Turnover on the CM in LTL	3,736,580     16,574,490</p>
<p>Number of transactions in</p>
<p>    bloc trades (BT)		   32		26</p>
<p>    Turnover of BT in LTL	    3,683,140     6,632,020</p>
<p>    Supply of shares per week	30,654,173    40,687,930</p>
<p>    Demand of shares per week	3,263,860     3,570,496</p>
<p>Turnover of shares</p>
<p>    on CM per week in LTL	    2,748,150     3,442,880</p>
<p>    in BT per week in LTL	    3,683,149     6,632,020</p>
<p>The number of transactions</p>
<p>    in government T bills	    6		 28</p>
<p>The turnover of government</p>
<p>    T-bills in LTL per week	  988,440	 13,131,610</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom + 370 2 22 35 17</p>
